tasks.contract:
Implement MCP in crates/adrian-api/src/mcp/ (and a thin wrapper in adrian-bin for the stdio proxy).

TRANSPORT: JSON-RPC 2.0 over HTTP at POST /mcp on the same axum router and same port as REST. Support the streamable-HTTP subset needed by coding agents: a single JSON-RPC request per POST, JSON response with content-type application/json, and `Accept: application/json, text/event-stream` tolerated by responding with JSON. Do not implement SSE streaming of partial results; return one complete JSON-RPC response per request. Return 400 with a JSON-RPC error object for malformed envelopes. Support batch arrays by processing sequentially.

PROTOCOL METHODS: initialize (return protocolVersion "2025-06-18", capabilities.tools = {}, serverInfo {name:"adrian", version}), notifications/initialized (204), ping, tools/list, tools/call. Return JSON-RPC error -32601 for unknown methods, -32602 for invalid params, -32603 for internal.

TOOLS (exact names, input schemas via serde_json json! and advertised in tools/list):
  adr_search { query: string, project?: string, status?: string, limit?: integer (default 5, max 50) }
  adr_get { id?: string, project?: string, number?: integer }   (exactly one of id or project+number)
  adr_list { project?: string, status?: string, limit?: integer (default 20, max 100) }
  adr_submit { project: string, external_ref: string, source: string, scopes?: string[], actor: string, idempotency_key?: string }
  adr_similar { id: string, limit?: integer (default 5, max 50) }
  adr_transition { id: string, to: string, reason?: string, actor: string }
  adr_context_for { path: string, project?: string, limit?: integer (default 10, max 50) }

Each tool returns content: [{ type: "text", text: <compact JSON> }] plus `isError: false`. On failure return isError: true with a readable message rather than a JSON-RPC error, per MCP convention for tool-level failures.

SAFETY RULE, enforce in code: adr_submit from any actor always creates the ADR with status `proposed` and never `accepted`, regardless of what the source front matter says. Only adr_transition can move an ADR to `accepted`. Write this as an explicit check with a test.

TOOL DESCRIPTIONS: each tool's description in tools/list must be a single actionable sentence written for an LLM consumer, stating when to use it, e.g. "Search architectural decisions by natural language; returns decisions with the matching sections and scores."

STDIO PROXY: `adrian mcp-stdio --url http://127.0.0.1:8080 [--token T]` reads newline-delimited JSON-RPC from stdin, forwards each to the daemon's /mcp, and writes the response to stdout. It must not buffer or reorder, must exit 0 on stdin EOF, and must log to stderr only (stdout is the protocol channel).

Worker MAY run `cargo test -p adrian-api mcp` and a manual pipe test of the stdio proxy against a running daemon. Keep unit tests hermetic with a stub daemon.
